      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-04T13:24:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This prevents having an executable in the APK, but doesn\u0027t (rightfully) prevent shared libraries, right?",
      "revId": "cc339a1978ee108ae5d11b60682a6458d05e6059",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f67691f2_bf1f33fe",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-04T13:40:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "noexec prevents libraries being loaded too.\n\nI\u0027m now confused as to the behaviour I\u0027m aiming for. I was understanding that these extra APKs were just going to be a means to make a tree of data files available within the VM, those files would contain untrusted input data and the payload would be responsible carefully accessing, measuring, validating them as is required by the use case.\n\nBut you\u0027re suggesting here that the extra APKs should be a way to load extra code into the VMs for the payload to execute? How would that interaction work? I\u0027d like to understand properly to tell which parts microdroid_manager should be responsible for and which parts the payload should be responsible for.",
      "parentUuid": "903c5a18_25bb6119",
      "revId": "cc339a1978ee108ae5d11b60682a6458d05e6059",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "485c8d44_6ede7006",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-04T13:59:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then I think it\u0027s the choice of the user who decides whether to allow executable or not in the extra APKs.\n\n\u003e How would that interaction work?\n\nWell, the main APK could locate a file in the extra APK via `/mnt/extra-apk/\u003cnum\u003e`? Yeah, having number in the path doesn\u0027t look good (`num` should actually have been `package_name`) and we currently don\u0027t have such a use case, but I think this CL is too restrictive for the future.",
      "parentUuid": "f67691f2_bf1f33fe",
      "revId": "cc339a1978ee108ae5d11b60682a6458d05e6059",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "823628a2_5ad0aa43",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-04T14:04:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that it blocks loading shared libraries, and that that is a good thing.\n\nThis is for config APKs. Code being run inside the VM should be part of the VM identity.",
      "parentUuid": "f67691f2_bf1f33fe",
      "revId": "cc339a1978ee108ae5d11b60682a6458d05e6059",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "33bae6eb_b300f547",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-04T14:27:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "By interaction, I meant more who is responsible for the loading, verification adding to dynamic linker search path etc.\n\nWe either have to say:\n  1) extra APK are pure inputs data, as this CL assumes, or\n  2) extra APKs are part of the payload itself.\n\nIf we want both, then we can start with 1), as that is how compos uses it for build_manifest.pb, and when there\u0027s a need for 2) we can add another microdroid config for that case.\n\nIf we just want 2) then I\u0027ll have to back to trying to pass build_manifest.pb to compos without BuildManifest.apk.",
      "parentUuid": "823628a2_5ad0aa43",
      "revId": "cc339a1978ee108ae5d11b60682a6458d05e6059",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
